			<div class="content" id="post-content-1901979">
									

<p>I am open to suggestions about further additions to the experiment log, but it is not open for anyone to make additions to it.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>1. I will accept either idea suggestions or fully-formatted log entries, but please put them in collapsibles either way. That means the suggestion should come in the following form, <strong>without the spaces between the brackets</strong>:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>[ [collapsible show=”WHATEVER YOU WANT THE RED TEXT THAT YOU CLICK ON TO BE” hide=”Hide”] ]</p>
<p>WHATEVER YOU WOULD LIKE TO SUGGESTING</p>
<p>[ [/collapsible] ]</p>
</blockquote>
<p>1.a. The whole point of the joke is that these are <em>subverted porn tropes.</em> The suggestion needs to be a situation reflected in common pornographic narratives (i.e. “oh, the plumber's here! Hope he can <em>fix my pipes</em>”). However, the suggestion needs to conclude with something completely nonsexual and unexpected. Boring even works, at that point, as long as it's amusingly boring. Bonus points if it's empowering to the female protagonists.<br />
1.b. Any porn works, so long as it has tropes to subvert. (That would be all the kinds I know about, at least.)</p>
<p>2. If you want to suggest a fully-formatted log, please use the format already in the log.<br />
3. Please give me a name of a researcher who you want to identify as being responsible for the experiment. This is the form for which your contribution will be acknowledged.<br />
3.a. Please make that name not be stupid.<br />
4. Please do not be offended if your suggestion is not used. There are many possible options; I may not have seen it, I may not have had the time, or I may not have liked it. Either way, bumping it will not make me be inclined to look kindly upon it.</p>
</div>
</div>
